    "background_story": "Hailey was a bright and curious student, but she had one major flaw: she was absolutely terrible at math. No matter how hard she tried, she just couldn't seem to grasp even the simplest concepts. Her classmates would often tease her, calling her a 'dunce' behind her back. But Hailey refused to let their jokes get her down. Instead, she worked twice as hard to excel in other subjects, discovering a hidden talent for writing and art. She became the editor of the school newspaper and even landed a few local art competitions. Despite her struggles with math, Hailey proved that being a 'dunce' in one area didn't define her entire intelligence or worth. She learned to laugh at herself and focus on her strengths, becoming a confident and well-rounded individual.",
